# MamayLM Gemma-3 12B IT v2.0 (Ukrainian) - Optimized for Bethesda Starfield Translation
# Base model: Gemma-3 12B IT, fine-tuned by INSAIT Institute for Ukrainian language
# Source: https://huggingface.co/INSAIT-Institute/MamayLM-Gemma-3-12B-IT-v2.0-GGUF

# IMPORTANT — parameter precedence:
#   The bethesda-strings-editor application overrides these options on every
#   API call (values here apply only to direct `ollama run` invocations):
#     temperature, num_ctx, num_predict, top_k, top_p, repeat_penalty, stop, system
#
#   These options are NOT overridden — the Modelfile values stay active during
#   API calls too:
#     min_p, repeat_last_n
#
#   The app sends a sampling knob only when the model's own profile in
#   OllamaWorker.MODEL_CONFIGS defines it. The "mamaylm" profile (matched by any
#   name starting `mamaylm`) defines top_k 64, top_p 0.95 and repeat_penalty,
#   but not min_p or repeat_last_n.
#
# To build from this file:
#   1. Download a GGUF from the model card above and point FROM at it.
#   2. ollama create mamaylm-gemma3-12b-v2.0 -f Modelfile.mamaylm
#   3. Select the model in the app's Settings -> Ollama. Keep the `mamaylm`
#      prefix in the name so the app's tuning profile applies.

FROM /path/to/MamayLM-Gemma-3-12B-IT-v2.0.Q4_K_M.gguf

# ── Chat template (Gemma 3) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same as Modelfile's, without the <|think|> guard: Gemma 3 (and so MamayLM)
# has no thinking mode.
TEMPLATE "{{ if .System }}<start_of_turn>system
{{ .System }}<end_of_turn>
{{ end }}{{ if .Prompt }}<start_of_turn>user
{{ .Prompt }}<end_of_turn>
{{ end }}<start_of_turn>model
{{ .Response }}<end_of_turn>"

# ── System prompt (Bethesda Starfield Localization) ───────────────────────────
# Used ONLY when no system is provided in the API call (direct use).
SYSTEM "You are a professional Bethesda Starfield game localization translator. Translate the given text into Ukrainian only. Output ONLY the translated text — no explanations, notes, or commentary. Preserve all formatting tokens exactly as written: <Alias=...>, <Token...>, <Global...>, %s, %d, {variable}, <br>, <font ...>, <mag>, <dur>, <relat=...>, <basename=...>, <repetitions>, [[TK_...]], [[STRUCT_BREAK_SGL_N]], [[STRUCT_BREAK_DBL_N]]. For square brackets: preserve input-binding tokens ([Attack], [Jump], [Sprint], etc.) and NPC name/variable tokens ([Name], [Andreja], [Vasco]) unchanged. Translate dialogue-choice tokens ([Lie], [Persuade], [Flirt], etc.) keeping the brackets. Translate ALL-CAPS status codes ([CANCELED], [REDACTED], [DELIVERED], etc.) to Ukrainian equivalents. Write distinctly Ukrainian — not a Russian transliteration. Use Ukrainian-specific vocabulary where it diverges from Russian (наразі not сейчас, завдяки not благодаря). Always close guillemet quotation marks: every opening « must have a matching closing »."

# ── Generation parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Temperature: model author recommends 1.0 (fine-tuned at this value).
# The application overrides this to 0.1 at runtime for deterministic output.
PARAMETER temperature 1.0

# Context window: 16 384 tokens covers all Bethesda string types, including
# books and terminal logs.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

# Maximum output tokens per request.
PARAMETER num_predict 4096

# Sampling — model author recommendations.
PARAMETER top_k 64
PARAMETER top_p 0.95

# min_p: drops tokens whose probability is below 2% of the top token's.
PARAMETER min_p 0.02

# Repeat penalty: light repetition control, safe for highly inflected Ukrainian.
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.1

# Repeat window: 256 tokens covers most Bethesda strings without overhead.
PARAMETER repeat_last_n 256

# ── Stop tokens ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Gemma turn-boundary markers
PARAMETER stop <end_of_turn>
PARAMETER stop <start_of_turn>
# Role-bleeding guards: prevent the model from faking a next user turn
PARAMETER stop user:
PARAMETER stop model:
PARAMETER stop <|user|>
PARAMETER stop <|model|>
